  "descriptions": {
    "quantity-theory-fixed-v-y:9a647b1312131cb74ce5a12f89f7ca18db35bb7101d077224f6d80626c55b31d": "Quantity-theory graph. The vertical axis is value of money, one divided by P; the horizontal axis is money supply M. Money demand MD slopes downward and curves toward the horizontal axis. Vertical MS1 is at 2,500 and meets MD at point a, at a money value of 2. Vertical MS2 is at 5,000 and meets MD at point b, at a money value of 1. Dashed horizontal guides mark 2 and 1. MS2 is to the right of MS1 and b is below and to the right of a. The vertical axis shows the reciprocal of the price level, not velocity V."
